<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">
        <p>A standard auction involves buyers continually placing higher bids until the auction closes. The highest bid when the auction ends is the winner.</p>
        <p>Lively offers competitive bidding mechanisms during our livestream sales. Find out everything you need to know about placing bids below.</p>

        <p><strong>On this page</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#">Before you bid</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">How to bid using the Bid button</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">How to type custom bids</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">After you win</a></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Before you bid</h2>
        <p>Ensure you have a payment method and shipping address attached to your account before placing a bid in a Live Show.</p>

        <h2>How to Bid</h2>
        <p>There are two primary methods for placing a bid in an auction:</p>

        <p><strong>Use the Bid button:</strong> Tap the colored Bid button at the bottom of your screen to place the next incremental bid.</p>
        
        <div class="text-center my-4">
            <img src="~/img/help_center/pre_bid.png" alt="Bid button example" class="img-fluid" style="border-radius: 12px; margin-bottom: 2rem;" />
        </div>

        <h2>Bid a custom amount and sending a bid</h2>
        <p>If you wish to bid significantly higher that the current increment to secure your purchase, you can enter a custom bid.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Tap the amount shown above the bid button to open your keypad.</li>
            <li>Input your custom maximum bid amount.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>To avoid accidental bids, you will be prompted to swipe or confirm your custom bid amount.</p>

        <div class="article-info-box">
            <strong>Remember:</strong> All bids are binding. Only bid what you are willing to pay. 
        </div>

        <div class="helpful-widget">
            <p>Was this article helpful?</p>
            <div class="helpful-buttons">
                <button type="button">Yes</button>
                <button type="button">No</button>
            </div>
            <span>158 out of 192 found this helpful</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
